{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385134-fanon-the-non-canon-and-houserule-thread","id":1385134,"title":"[Fanon] The non-canon and houserule thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-01T13:54:05-07:00","id":1385134,"title":"[Fanon] The non-canon and houserule thread","content":"A spinoff of the armor thread:<br /> <br /> Basically, here's a thread for sharing your non-canon and house-rules that you think would make interesting changes to V5 or V20 games.<br /> <br /> For the sake of avoiding a cheap joke, I shouldn't need to say, &quot;Replace everything in V5&quot; or something easily cheap. If you do want to give an alternate version of a new edition, though, feel free to list how you would have updated things.<br /> <br /> Just don't take any potshots at the previous edition or current one doing so. This is meant to be good fun. I've seen some interesting rules proposed in this forum and think a place to compile them would be good. Things like using Loresheets for Paths of Enlightenment and new flaws for Clans.<br /> <br /> Commentary is welcome on people's work but, again, keep it civil.<br /> <br /> Malkav will be watching.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T14:05:18-07:00","id":1385136,"title":"","content":"<b>General</b><br /> <br /> + Change the Lasombra Clan Flaw to only being invisible in mirrors. It doesn't affect security footage or photographs or videos but allows people to identify you as a vampire as they see you. I also would add silver as a vulnerability because it's kind of weaksauce with silver weapons causing aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> + Make Tzimisce clan are actually more the Dracula clan versus the Necroscope clan. Their weakness would remain the same but they would have Animalism, Blood Sorcery, and Protean as their Disciplines. They would be less about being flesh-obsessed serial killers and more about being creepy old world aristocrats.<br /> <br /> + Theo Bell is currently in hiding among the Anarchs. He's not on the Red List yet but that's because there's not been an opening in the past few years. The Camarilla has standing orders to eliminate him and he's someone with a vast bounty on his head.<br /> <br /> <b>V5</b><br /> <br /> + Make Vicissitude to be a Combo Discipline of Blood Sorcery and Protean. It also requires any permanent changes to be done to someone's flesh to be something that has to be done in a creepy laboratory set up for the process. No permanent deformation with a touch.<br /> <br /> + Create &quot;Elder Disciplines&quot; that are a separate roll from regular Disciplines,. They require Blood Potency of 5+ and a full 5 dots in the previous Disciplines are 1-5 rolls. Basically, they replace 6-10 Discipline levels but are a different rules system for using them.<br /> <br /> + Make a Path of Enlightenment Loresheet that allows you to do various actions without affecting your Humanity score or gaining humanity from it.<br /> <br /> + Make it a Loresheet that the Banu Haqim can substitute Presence or Celerity for Blood Sorcery. The ones who joined the Camarilla and survived were mostly the Magician caste.<br /> <br /> + Sabbat can use nonhumans as their Loresheets.<br /> <br /> <b>Classic</b><br /> <br /> + Get rid of Celerity as an extra-action as that's always made it the most broken discipline.<br /> <br /> + Overhaul the Thin Blood system so its not such a disaster. Thin Bloods can gain Disciplines of 1-3 but can only spend 1 blood point per round anyway, which is it's own restriction. They can also buy the 5pt merit of Daywalker that bestows immunity to the sun's curse. There's also a 2pt version that will make you immune to it for minutes rather than rounds so you can easily cross the street but not stay out indefinitely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-01-2020, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T15:05:17-07:00","id":1385139,"title":"","content":"<b>V5</b><br /> <br /> Get rid of the current Hecata bane and replace it with the homebrew one I posted somewhere here. Necromancers are affected by wards and abjurations as if they were ghosts themselves.<br /> <br /> Members of necromantic bloodlines (Giovanni, Samedi, Lamiae, etc) have always had their own banes, which vary by lineage; make these be mechanically Flaws taken by 95% of the bloodline (the 5% being outliers like the Premascine Giovanni embraced post-Augustus, which are very rare but do exist). Samedi are Repulsive, Nagaraja are Organovores, and so on. The painful bite is a two-point Flaw taken by Giovanni.<br /> <br /> &quot;Modern&quot; Hecata\u2014the ones with Auspex, Fortitude, Oblivion and no bloodline-specific Flaw\u2014are created by members of different bloodlines combining their vitae in the Embrace. They're not a thing that just happens; someone Embraced in the classic method will end up with their Sire's bloodline flaw 95% of the time. Previously-created Hecata also keep their flaws.<br /> <br /> The end result of these changes is that the Hecata work within the V5 system, but that the Family Reunion was purely a political/social alliance. (By RAW, the Reunion was mostly a political alliance, but also magically changed everyone's clan bane and discipline spread. Which feels a bit too meta.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T15:10:16-07:00","id":1385140,"title":"","content":"Hey! Leave the Necroscope clan alone! Ventrue and Lasombra already have creepy arsito covered, and Viscititude is nothing to do with Protean...unless Dominate and Presence should also be combined. Tzimisce are fine as they are, and Paths should not be Humanity, that was and remains the entire point of them, Humanity is a separate morality system from the paths, the changes made does all of them a gross disservice, and having tried it in a playtest does not work, it is not granular and nuanced enough.<br /> <br /> So my house rules: bring back Conscience/Self control, Conviction/Instinct and courage, they worked, as long as you actually used them, and make Humanity/Paths hard and rigid systems again, really focus on that aspect, not the game wrecking hunger system. <br /> <br /> Make combat more simulationist and stop trying to use one system to simulate every form of conflict, social engineering is not best represented by the same style of rolling used for a gun fight, or investigation, (WoD Combat was pretty good, not perfect by any means, but pretty good, do that for the other types of conflict as well, have the option to get really down in the weeds if you like)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T15:21:18-07:00","id":1385142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385134-fanon-the-non-canon-and-houserule-thread?p=1385140#post1385140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey! Leave the Necroscope clan alone! Ventrue and Lasombra already have creepy arsito covered, and Viscititude is nothing to do with Protean...unless Dominate and Presence should also be combined. Tzimisce are fine as they are, and Paths should not be Humanity, that was and remains the entire point of them, Humanity is a separate morality system from the paths, the changes made does all of them a gross disservice, and having tried it in a playtest does not work, it is not granular and nuanced enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if they renamed V5's Humanity to &quot;Morality&quot; or &quot;Consciousness&quot;?<br /> <br /> Serious question if it was just a measure of how far you were from the Beast.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T15:54:36-07:00","id":1385147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385134-fanon-the-non-canon-and-houserule-thread?p=1385142#post1385142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What if they renamed V5's Humanity to &quot;Morality&quot; or &quot;Consciousness&quot;?<br /> <br /> Serious question if it was just a measure of how far you were from the Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>No,. The entire system is to loose, and if you try to force the Sins, Tenets and Philosophy of a Path (including Humanity) onto the 3 Convictions, it flat doesn't work, let alone Chronicle Tenets not really working with characters on different Paths anyway (their a reason Vinicullum holds the Sabbat together, the Paths don't, sure Honorable Accord cares about Sect cohesion, Metamorphosis and Feral Heart don't) V5 choose to take the focus off the Intellect Vs animalistic conflict the original virtue system focused on, trying to turn it back with the tools provided doesn't work (and yes a good faith attempt was made). They decided to import touchstones/fetters, and the hunger mechanics, which completely alter the flavour of the setting, and the nature of degeneration, the two themes do not play nice with each other.<br /> <br /> The reason it didn't work was the lack of ability to assign import to the sins, what is worse, what matters more, what can be surrendered for an quiet unlife, that slow slide of beast I be lest Beast I become' doesn't fit with 3 convictions.<br /> <br /> So while renaming it would be nice, it doesn't solve the core issues.<br /> <br /> ( And yes I did complain way back when, when killing stopped being Humanity 2 sin ( iirc it was 2, with mass killing being 1). Paths should matter, trivialising Humanity hurt them all, and it showed from revised onwards)<br /> <br /> That is the core thematic issue I have, the rules issues don't help, because they compound on each other, if Path was handled amazingly I would suck up rules I don't like, and if the rules where amazing I would cope with bad paths, but both together is a deal breaker. (Hell I only played the Harry Dresden RPG onve, because I loathed the system that much, so their is a point where unfun mechanics kill a setting for me)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-01-2020, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T16:40:47-07:00","id":1385152,"title":"","content":"Replace VtM torpor with VtR torpor, and diablre of the young by the old treats the worst effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 05-03-2020, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T17:13:29-07:00","id":1385153,"title":"","content":"<b>V5</b><br /> <br /> 1. Allow multiple loresheets even a character creation.<br /> 2. Change the text for humanity 10. and clarify Humanity a bit it seems to be suffering form split personalities, but that is just my thoughts. i treat it as the yourself/beast scale which i sthe common interpretation for humanity. I also use Chipotle Chris' paths homebrew.<br /> 3. Non-human touchstone rules would be nice. I just allow them so long as they are not conceptual.<br /> 4. Roufuss rounds are a bit much. reduce the damage output to 2 with Agg for vampires.<br /> 5. Give optional movement rates for those that may wish to combat grid their combats. or at least have a guidance of how far they are moving. I use the same as V20 for basic movement (7)<br /> 6. Give 1 XP for the session, 1 for Ambition or desire advancement and 1 at end of every story which is typically every other session.<br /> 7. Though it is allowed in the rules I explicitly allow players to gain backgrounds with projects for free. but they do have to earn them with projects which are not automatic. enemies will mess with your projects.<br /> <br /> <b>V20</b><br /> <br /> 1. Add automatic damage as well. A Vampire should not be able to stuff a grenade down his trousers and possibly take no damage. no soak versus things you shouldn't be able to.<br /> 2. Set the net success form an automatic hit to 4-5 and auto damage to half damage dice + net hits.<br /> 3. Defense should be free to use once per round. Desperate Defense, from Mage of all places, should be allowed in Werewolf and Vampire.<br /> 4. The dodge target number for dodging a firearm at regular range is 7, they only list close range for some reason. technically this is a house rule.<br /> 5. Only give 3 XP max.<br /> <br /> Thats off the top of my head.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T17:37:00-07:00","id":1385155,"title":"","content":"Replace Animalism and Auspex with their namesakes from Vampire: The Requiem 2nd Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T19:30:27-07:00","id":1385173,"title":"","content":"As some of you know, I am always in the process of tinkering with the rules. The version I play now only strongly resembles either V20 or its predecessors. Listing all the changes would take a really long time and no one wants a wall of text anyway, so I'll limit myself to a link:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/g6yuikeoa903u2e/Degeneration%201-5%20Final-op.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/g6yuikeoa9...al-op.pdf?dl=0</a><br /> <br /> That's a 267 page compilation of the custom rules, although to be fair, 77 page of it is just Thaumaturgy and Necromancy (with all the attendant rituals). So if you skipped that part, it's just 190 pages.<br /> <br /> It's not the most current version, but it's the last &quot;complete&quot; version. I won't have v1.75 for another few months I think -- adding some advanced combat rules and making tweaks to a lot of the systems.<br /> <br /> Apologies to all who have seen this material before.<br /> <br /> PS - There's a plain blank white first page, so it may look like the document isn't loading. That's an artifact from the printing process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T21:21:49-07:00","id":1385184,"title":"","content":"Due to the actions and choices of a player character I allow new-ish Tremere character's who are in house Tremere to start as a former thinblood and keep access to thinblood alchemy at the cost of the first rouse check they make in a turn will require a second rouse check if it comes up a 1, they start with -1 humanity due to the guaranteed diablerie and either the suspect flaw, Any defectors from the house are pursued due to their rarity and the endangerment of one of the house's bigger secret advantages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T08:15:44-07:00","id":1385243,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Some of the many house rules I established at my table or plan to introduce in the future:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Multiple powers &amp; Diablerie:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Normaly every vampire is restricted to 5 powers per discipline. There is only one way out of that: Diablerie. Whenever a vampire successfully diablerizes another vampire, they receive one additional 'slot' for one discipline power of a clan discipline of the victim. The level of the additional power 'slot' cannot exceed the blood potency of the victim. The 'slot' does not count towards the current discipline level of the user.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Example:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Brad the Banu Haqim surprises (Obfuscate 3) and sucks dry Mitch the Ministry vampire. Mitch's blood potency was 3. If Brad wanted, he could gain an extra level 1, level 2 or level 3 power (exceeding the ultimate limit of five powers per discipline) of either Presence, Obfuscate or Protean. He chooses Obfuscate and weeks later he spends the 15 xp to learn Mask of a Thousand Faces, besides already knowing Ghost in the Machine. His effective level of obfuscate is still 3.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Diablerie &amp; Character creation:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Depending on background story, a player may start the game with a character that has commited diablerie. Standard character creation rules apply. At the end, all the neccessary rolls for commiting diablerie are done, including humanity loss and potential XP (and/or generation) gain. Resulting XP may be invested before the game starts, if enough time has passed.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Armor:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Being prepared is of value, even for vampires. Armor serves a dual function. It can transform up to its armor rating of aggravated damage into superficial damage per hit or it can provide up to half of its armor rating in one-time temporary health levels. One cannot combine armor to do both.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Once temporary health levels are filled with either damage, the armor loses its protective capacity and needs to be replaced.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Example:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Harry the Hunter (a mortal) is wearing a kevlar vest (armor rating 4) when getting shot (4 levels of aggravated damage). The vest transforms the damage into superficial damage, which is halved to 2 levels of superficial damge.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bill the Brujah is wearing a heavy lether jacket (armor rating 2) when getting sliced by feral weapons from Gary the Gangrel (6 levels of unhalved superficial damage). His jacket absorbes one level of those and is ripped to shreds. Bill also suffers the remaining 5 levels of superficial damage.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Victor the Ventrue is wearing military grade armor (armor rating 6) to take down Willy the Wight when he is bitten by the frenzying vampire (2 levels of aggravated damage). The armor absorbes those to levels and still has one level to absorb without causing any damage to Victor. Willy has not pierced the skin and cannot start feeding.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ghouls:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Vampires are usually only able to bestow upon their ghouls the first level and power of their highest level discipline. If multiple disciplines share the highest level, the vampire can choose between those.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If a vampire wishes to bestow the first level and power of a different discipline they know, they have to have fed on blood of intense resonance of the intended discipline.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">There are however dyscrasias that let the vampire choose freely between all their disciplines.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Presence:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The restrictions of use in combat for powers like Dread Gaze and Majesty is not exhaustive. Powers like Daunt and Eyes of the Serpent may also be used in combat.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dominate:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Submerged Directive can be used to implant lasting commands that work repeatedly when the stimulus reoccurs instead of one-timed triggered mesmerizms. Such commands may be resisted every time.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25558-pangur-b\u00e1n","name":"Pangur B\u00e1n","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T10:04:33-07:00","id":1385261,"title":"","content":"V20<br /> <br /> Rules<br /> -Don't roll for damage or soak in combat, just take half. After you get used to it, makes combat far quicker. When dealing with damage where 'take half' isn't appropriate (Fire, Sunlight, special powers) 1's and 10s' do not subtract or add extra successes. <br /> -Stamina soaks aggravated damage that isn't fire/sunlight/faith. IE claws, burning swords, <br /> -Fortitude adds dice to resisting getting knocked down, it also makes one immune to electricity if it exceeds the effects. <br /> -Big guns do more damage, armour soaks more. <br /> -Getting one success on an attack roll means you've hit a less desirable target (IE a limb when you aim for the body, the head when you aim for the eyes) Getting five successes means you hit something more favourable than you originally intended. 2 and 4 might have this effect depending on context. <br /> -You can work towards regaining humanity without XP expenditure. <br /> -During downtime, you can use your time to either accumulate backgrounds, regain humanity, learn rituals. If you want to 'train' at all without spending xp I'll give you a merit to reduce/remove the penalty for not having a skill. <br /> <br /> Fluff<br /> Generally I try to keep as close to the sourcebooks as possible except when dealing with cities, individuals and dates. Most of my fluff is 'The logical continuation of...' rather than some whacky idea i've made. <br /> -It's getting easier to learn blood magic thanks to the information age, and the Tremere are very sore about it. <br /> -The Tremere want to teach the path of blood first because each level needs a tutor, keeping learners dependent on the clan if they want to advance their thaumaturgy. In light of the modern era, they've started to cede the first two levels of thaumaturgy in order to spread anti-tech rituals for the good of the masquerade. If the Tremere won't give, you could ask the Nosferatu... but that's a darker hole to crawl into. <br /> -Most infernalists don't get caught. There are more of them than you realise. <br /> -Elders in the cam really, really hate vicissitude. It doesn't matter if you want to use it for good and noble purposes, they really hate it. There are many secret societies in the cam, and a few in the anarchs, dedicated to stomping vicissitude out, much to the chargrin of neonates everywhere enamoured by modern cosmetic surgery. It's part traumatic experience, part religion, and part paranoia. While Vicissitude isn't actually evil, practicing vicissitude can be a great drain on humanity as it requires a lot of 'research material' and it's quite hard to hit the undo with surgery on a living thing. When the downtown strays disappear, the people gotta start watching out. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T11:34:29-07:00","id":1385278,"title":"","content":"With diablerie being framed as the ancients' trap for the young and the unwary in the evolving metaplot, maybe the vampire who feeds on another should have to make dice rolls <i>to stop</i> instead of dice rolls to keep going. The paradigm goes from framing the diablerist as someone strong enough to seize power to someone too weak to resist temptation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T11:59:56-07:00","id":1385280,"title":"","content":"Arguably not so much non-canon as retro from a V20 perspective, but I would grandfather in the 2nd Edition rules about soaking aggravated damage (roll Stamina + Fortitude against sources like claws and bites; Fortitude only against Fire and Sunlight) and the Revised rules about countering mages' spells (roll Thaumaurgy rating + dots in Thaumaturgical Countermagic vs. diff. of mage's Willpower; 2 successes negate one success). The former avoids handing werewolves an automatic &quot;I win&quot; button for any fight with vampires while still giving them the advantage most of the time, and the latter makes resisting true magick a function of practical mystical expertise and raw supernatural power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T13:00:05-07:00","id":1385287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385134-fanon-the-non-canon-and-houserule-thread?p=1385280#post1385280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arguably not so much non-canon as retro from a V20 perspective, but I would grandfather in the 2nd Edition rules about soaking aggravated damage (roll Stamina + Fortitude against sources like claws and bites; Fortitude only against Fire and Sunlight).</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this and will be poaching it for my game, but what do you do about Serpentis rank 3?<br /> <br /> It\u2019s main ability in V20 is allowing you to use Stamina to soak agg from teeth, claws, etc., but not sunlight, fire or magic energies. Without that benefit it\u2019s mostly just spend blood to turn ugly and get -1 diff to soak rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T13:34:57-07:00","id":1385296,"title":"","content":"<b>V5</b><br /> <br /> One area I've experimented with for Elders and Methuselahs in V5 is the idea of the <b>Withering</b> and statlessness. Basically, if you attend the Gehenna War and answer the Beckoning then you are going to keep your 6+ stats or Elder Disciplines. The Call of the Antediluvians is such that answering it promises you to keep your level of power if you survive their judgement and join with the battle against their enemies.<br /> <br /> If you DON'T answer the Beckoning then you are going to slowly start losing your Disciplines over 5 and gradually become as weak as an Ancilla or at most an 8th level Elder of significant power. The only way around this status is regular diablerie either of Thin Bloods or stronger vampires. Just drinking vampire blood can forestall the Beckoning but not the power loss.<br /> <br /> This has had an enormous affect on those Beckoned vampires who have stayed behind because even if its weak enough for them to resist, the loss of their upper tier powers has caused the Camarilla to lose battles they would have otherwise curbstomped the Second Inqusition or Anarchs with.<br /> <br /> Some Elders have ALSO returned from the Gehenna War with few memories of what happened there but full powers. <b>Tyler</b>, for example, has returned from Carthage with no memory of events but far stronger powers. An encounter with her that goes violent will be summarized as, &quot;You lose.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T18:28:12-07:00","id":1385498,"title":"","content":"Still brainstorming but a few things that came to me as I was reading over the thread...<br /> <br /> \u2022Virtues <br /> -Conscious: as it currently stands mechanically (at least V20 and prior), I'd say that 'Justification' might make a bit more sense to describe its primary function. However on the other hand, I can see the argument that succeeding on conscious is about still feeling bad for doing something wrong, so I suppose it depends on how you handle the virtue, because I've definitely seen it run as essential 'Justification' at times.<br /> <br /> \u2022Morality<br /> -I think more of a point could be made about how torturous, radically altering, and difficult adapting to a Path of Enlightenment from Humanity should be. For all vampires really, but especially for the Sabbat where priests should be constantly struggling to keep their charges from crumbling into insanity or becoming wights from the strain of their existence.<br /> <br /> -Masquerade; another morality point is something of a philosophical one. Whether consciously or subconsciously, a character's morality is their mental self-image that they construct to keep at bay the reality of monstrosity. That doesn't mean morality is a condemnation though. I think that stories of the desperate emulation of humanity in the face of existential and perhaps inevitable degeneration are beautiful. This is why one of my core philosophical themes for VtM is the idea of 'Becoming the Mask'.<br /> <br /> \u2022Comedy<br /> -Bloody food; I don't know where this headcanon started but for a chronicle using comedic elements I would definitely consider implementing it. The idea is that vampires can eat food thoroughly mixed with blood. Ridiculous? Yes. But darkly so and sometimes that's the vibe you want.<br /> <br /> \u2022Characters<br /> -Washington D.C. has steadily seen more and more Romanesque architectural design over the past half century, even more then its famous original monuments. Wonder why...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T18:30:15-07:00","id":1385702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385134-fanon-the-non-canon-and-houserule-thread?p=1385287#post1385287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this and will be poaching it for my game, but what do you do about Serpentis rank 3?<br /> <br /> It\u2019s main ability in V20 is allowing you to use Stamina to soak agg from teeth, claws, etc., but not sunlight, fire or magic energies. Without that benefit it\u2019s mostly just spend blood to turn ugly and get -1 diff to soak rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also gives an extra die of bite damage and allows the vampire to squeeze through openings big enough for their head to pass through. Those three benefits together have enough utility for a three dot power in my book. Without the retro houserule, it's way overpowered for that level\u2014could be the equivalent of up to five dots of Fortitude (more if you let blood-boosted Stamina count) <b>plus</b> easier soak difficulties <b>plus</b> extra damage <b>plus</b> wriggling through narrow spaces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","user":"Matt the Bruins fan","date":". 05-04-2020, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T18:04:04-07:00","id":1388805,"title":"","content":"So *sigh*<br /> <br /> I was being a bit of a nerd and No One of Consequences reviews of the old 1e clan character concepts and thinking about what their equivalents would be in the modern zeitgeist of the 2010s.<br /> <br /> I ended up with ideas like the Waxed-Mustache Hipster Toreador and the Butch-in-Flannel Gangrel, when my mind drifted to the Malkavians and I was suddenly struck with a horrible dawning realization.<br /> <br /> Certainly Malkavian characters could work well to analyze things like the pursuit of constant gratification on Millenia psyche, the noedaidistic nihilism of Gen Z, the worn down working poor, shaken veterans of the War on Terror, and plenty of other things.<br /> <br /> Yet as certain as anything, staring me in the back of my mind's eye...<br /> <br /> That some Malkavians... particularly those of the Dementation bloodline... and considering the obvious allegories created by the nature of the Malkavians Madness Network.<br /> <br /> Well modern Malkavians would have to be the masters of memetic mutation. That genuinely unintentional alliteration aside, the thought struck me when I was thinking about how Malkavians would be good at rooting out old and damning tweets and that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> But like...<br /> <br /> Now that I've seen it, I honestly can't unsee it.<br /> <br /> Some Malkavians would have to be meme lords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T14:18:30-07:00","id":1389068,"title":"","content":"For V20:<br /> <br /> \u2022 I seconded eliminating extra attacks. I'm toying with the idea of a house rule that would make Celerity like Potence and just give auto-successes for a blood point, or extra movement. For Werewolves, they could spend a point of rage for auto successes to Dex and/or Str, like V20 Celerity or Potence.<br /> <br /> \u2022 At least make soaking automatic instead of a roll - there are some quick combat rules in Dark Ages V20 that can be adapted pretty easily.<br /> <br /> \u2022 I stole the V5 hybrid Blood Potency/Generation rules for my V20 game. It seems to be working out ok.<br /> <br /> \u2022 I also grabbed the Predator Styles from V5, but as part of the character concept, not character creation. I think it's a helpful idea to think about how a new vampire might actually be feeding, especially for new players.<br /> <br /> \u2022 I also like the idea of V5 Resonances or something like them as bonuses for drinking supernatural critter blood, or maybe for highly dramatic mortals.<br /> <br /> For V5, I haven't played but have been thinking of ways to tinker with the system. Here are some ideas:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Limit Messy Criticals to actions fueled by blood, rather than just any action<br /> <br /> \u2022 Armor when not applied to Aggravated damage reduces superficial damage by half it's value; so armor does something for superficial damage<br /> <br /> \u2022 Allow non-human touchstones. Maybe a merit to skip them entirely if a player really doesn't want one<br /> <br /> \u2022 Drinking supernatural blood slakes all hunger - this is kinda implied in the Methuselah's Thirst merit, but not spelled out anywhere that I could find<br /> <br /> \u2022 Allowing multiple powers for Disciplines at levels that Blood Potency gives a re-roll to the rouse checks for.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Consider high/low tiers for the Chronicle Tenants. If taken to the absurd, vampires could be sent into Wassail from things like snitching too much or failing to support true love if certain tenants are used.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Consider something else than automatic stains for Embracing or Blood Bonding. That seems like a port over of the Requiem willpower hits for embracing or creating ghouls, which as I understand are meant to limit mass embraces or ghoul abuse. With the freeform Chronicle Tenants, having these automatic stains doesn't seem to fit well the the idea of open tenants, and may even clash with some tenants, depending. I feel like temporary Blood Potency hits (minus the Bane penalties and such) could work. <br /> <br /> \u2022 This might be too supers with fangs, but I miss vampires with higher than human stats, at least attributes. Maybe give some sort of Blood Potency bonus to attribute rolls? <br /> <br /> More of V5 wish list than rule changes:<br /> <br /> \u2022 More advanced combat rules would be nice, something like the WoD Armory books from CoD<br /> <br /> \u2022 More powers for Disciplines that do not require rouse checks - I have a personal preference for passive abilities or unlimited use, and I like how in V20 most of the disciplines allow for this style of play<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25885-ozymandias242","name":"Ozymandias242","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T19:55:15-07:00","id":1389170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 This might be too supers with fangs, but I miss vampires with higher than human stats, at least attributes. Maybe give some sort of Blood Potency bonus to attribute rolls? </div> </div> </div>To my thinking, this is filled by a combo of the bonus dice Blood Potency gives to Discipline rolls, and the fact that vampires can now boost <i>all</i> Attributes with a Blood Surge, not just the Physical ones. It ties such superhuman competence more to a deliberate exercise of supernatural power rather than low generation vampires having higher default trait maximums and just being passively better, but that's actually an improvement for me. No more trying to rationalize how a vampire with a static, unchanging form is able to make itself stronger or tougher over the years apart from use of its clearly vampiric powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T21:17:16-07:00","id":1389181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385134-fanon-the-non-canon-and-houserule-thread?p=1389170#post1389170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To my thinking, this is filled by a combo of the bonus dice Blood Potency gives to Discipline rolls, and the fact that vampires can now boost <i>all</i> Attributes with a Blood Surge, not just the Physical ones. It ties such superhuman competence more to a deliberate exercise of supernatural power rather than low generation vampires having higher default trait maximums and just being passively better, but that's actually an improvement for me. No more trying to rationalize how a vampire with a static, unchanging form is able to make itself stronger or tougher over the years apart from use of its clearly vampiric powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>*sigh* This is why I don't like certain aspects of the White Wolf lore that got casually created without real thought. Like vampires being &quot;static&quot; when the most famous vampire constantly varies in age, and is a constant shapeshifter, and is established as growing in strength as he ages. Or vampires being &quot;spiritually dead&quot;, when they've so often been associated with necromancy and dark nature stuff like storms and pestilent animal swarms. Spiritually dead makes them sound like technological types or evil lawyers. White Wolf just inserts things that cause more problems than benefits without thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T22:23:19-07:00","id":1389197,"title":"","content":"My impression (and I don't know for sure as I came onboard in 2nd Edition) was that the spiritually dead stuff came out of Werewolf with its animistic umbral-spirit-in-every-box-of-cornflakes approach. As for the static physical form bit, I believe the game follows the Anne Rice model rather than Stoker's in that respect. Anyhoo, the newer mechanics suit my priorities for the game fine for the most part; I think the Humanity system as the only option and its requirement of Touchstones are about the only aspect I have a real problem with. (We won't go into my much bigger objections to metaplot contrivances and gameplay style railroading...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T22:27:35-07:00","id":1389198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385134-fanon-the-non-canon-and-houserule-thread?p=1389181#post1389181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *sigh* This is why I don't like certain aspects of the White Wolf lore that got casually created without real thought. Like vampires being &quot;static&quot; when the most famous vampire constantly varies in age, and is a constant shapeshifter, and is established as growing in strength as he ages. Or vampires being &quot;spiritually dead&quot;, when they've so often been associated with necromancy and dark nature stuff like storms and pestilent animal swarms. Spiritually dead makes them sound like technological types or evil lawyers. White Wolf just inserts things that cause more problems than benefits without thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's because vampires are mechanically superior and role-playingly cursed. Vampires have immortality, super-strength, super-senses, and a variety of odder abilities. They also get essentially an orgasm/heroin rush everytime they feed.<br /> <br /> Suggesting that they suffer not just homicidal rage episodes when they get mad but a variety of other mental and spiritual ailments due to their curse is fun to roleplay without crippling character abilities.<br /> <br /> One of the reasons the Vampire Chronicles became....silly....was vampirism lost all of its curse element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T03:48:13-07:00","id":1389234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385134-fanon-the-non-canon-and-houserule-thread?p=1389181#post1389181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *sigh* This is why I don't like certain aspects of the White Wolf lore that got casually created without real thought. Like vampires being &quot;static&quot; when the most famous vampire constantly varies in age, and is a constant shapeshifter, and is established as growing in strength as he ages. Or vampires being &quot;spiritually dead&quot;, when they've so often been associated with necromancy and dark nature stuff like storms and pestilent animal swarms. Spiritually dead makes them sound like technological types or evil lawyers. White Wolf just inserts things that cause more problems than benefits without thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Vampires being &quot;spiritually dead&quot; has something I've taken to mean something else; Vampires are spiritually aligned with the dead. If you imagine werewolves and the umbra to be Yang, Vampires and ghosts are Yin. Humans are in the middle of the road and get a little bit of both, Vampires see a lot more ghosts than humans but see a lot less of the umbral spirits because they've been polarized the other way. Similarly, Lupines have a harder time taking notice of ghosts. Of course, werewolves have ghost specialists (there are umbral spirits of death too) whilst vampires have people that interact with spirits IE Thaumaturges, but they're innately pushed towards opposite ends of the spectrum. <br /> <br /> Vampires being static. <br /> One explanation: How come all these people have been undead for 100 years but they're not all AAA characters? They should be black belts/financial wizards/actual wizard/enthralling conversationalists/super spy scientists! I only get 1xp every X amount of downtime but surely if i used all that time training... <br /> <br /> A better explanation. <br /> people's childhoods mean more to them than later years. When you're five years old, turning six will mean 1/6th of your life so far has passed, and when you don't remember the first year or two, it's even more prominent. When you're 49, the next year will be 1/50th of your life. When you're 300... Your strongest memories are going to be biased towards the start of your life. The lessons learned at six are going to have a lot more impact than the ones at 49 or 300.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T04:57:37-07:00","id":1389252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385134-fanon-the-non-canon-and-houserule-thread?p=1389197#post1389197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My impression (and I don't know for sure as I came onboard in 2nd Edition) was that the spiritually dead stuff came out of Werewolf with its animistic umbral-spirit-in-every-box-of-cornflakes approach. As for the static physical form bit, I believe the game follows the Anne Rice model rather than Stoker's in that respect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe you're right on both counts.<br /> <br /> It should be noted that the idea of vampires as essentially unchanging has always had a place in the Anarchs vs Camarilla plot; the young coterie's ability to do an end run around an antagonistic elder with their fancy understanding of the modern world was the most important edge the youngsters had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T10:48:36-07:00","id":1389359,"title":"","content":"V20 Dhampirs that where born from a Golconda Vampire above the 15th Generation can increase their disciples to the half natural maximum (rounded down) of their parent. If the parents where two Golconda vampires the lower generation will be used and the natural limit will be rounded up instead.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T11:51:39-07:00","id":1389386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385134-fanon-the-non-canon-and-houserule-thread?p=1389234#post1389234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Vampires being &quot;spiritually dead&quot; has something I've taken to mean something else; Vampires are spiritually aligned with the dead. If you imagine werewolves and the umbra to be Yang, Vampires and ghosts are Yin. Humans are in the middle of the road and get a little bit of both, Vampires see a lot more ghosts than humans but see a lot less of the umbral spirits because they've been polarized the other way. Similarly, Lupines have a harder time taking notice of ghosts. Of course, werewolves have ghost specialists (there are umbral spirits of death too) whilst vampires have people that interact with spirits IE Thaumaturges, but they're innately pushed towards opposite ends of the spectrum.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I view them as well. They are inherently part of the necromancy end of the spiritual spectrum. They are spiritually about death rather than spiritually dead. But that doesn't generally seem to be what White Wolf has meant. Instead, they seem to push the idea that vampires are like Terminators and evil bureaucrats: creatures who are The Man and devoid of spirituality of any sort. It's the cool rebels and the cool exotic supernatural species who have the spirituality. Not the vampires, they're The Man and The Man is spiritually dead. Of course, they also frequently contradict themselves, but that's the subtext of a lot of what they say.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T12:47:36-07:00","id":1390605,"title":"","content":"So I've been thinking about vampiric history some, because my brain likes to think about how the qualities and traits of those earliest vampires established trends and history that paved the way for the vampiric setting we have today in the World of Darkness. So, looking towards the near beginning, most especially in Egypt, Mesopotamia, China, and the Indus-River Valley; here's some things that came to me...<br /> <br /> VAMPIRES OF THE BRONZE AGE<br /> <br /> \u2022Blood Divinity<br /> -You are the children of gods. Any Vampire of this period is like the legendary Gilgamesh yet even greater. Not only are you the child of a divinity, you yourself are now an eternal deity, like your progenitor even if somewhat weaker. You may hear your sires whisper of the half-remembered tales of One God that haunted The First, He Who Sired Us All; yet those stories are fragments and shadows after millennia of death and deluge.<br /> <br /> The vampires of these nights, who I treat as most likely being a majority range of the 4th-7th generation with the 5th and 6th being predominant, I divide into three categories.<br /> <br /> --High Gods: These are the ancients. Those who rule in the dark cities of the underworld or in the heavenly realms above, far from us. They are unspeably powerful and their whims and wills are what shall shape all of the world that is to come. Their presence defined empires and entire lands. These are the third and fourth generations, the highest progenitor gods that we all must worship, though one worships their own grand-father most highly, as is right and just.<br /> <br /> --Temple Gods: These are the beings that stalk the night and shape the world with their steps. They claim great city-states as their domains and they are housed within the temples of those cities. They are revered as gods upon the earth, sat beside-above-or upon the very throne of the city. Their temples are wetted with the whole cities sacrifices and in turn the temple god guarantees the cities prosperity in accordance to its own will and power. These gods rival and battle the temple gods of other cities with only the common ties of a great progenitor being respected and even then rarely. When these gods are righteous and powerful, their wills create empires and they become one step below the high gods. Yet when they fail their cities fall to ruin and they are dragged from their temples to be trophies or sacrifices to the temple gods of the victors. These are largely the fifth and sixth generations.<br /> <br /> --Shrine Gods: These gods are weaker then those ancient ones that made them yet stronger then any man. They dwell alone within villages afield or as priests and lesser gods of those temple gods that command their home cities. Families and households often cherish their shrine gods, many of whom are revered ancestors. They are given sacrifices to keep them strong and so they might represent their patrons interests to the courts of the gods. These young gods are largely the sixth and seventh generations, as well as the eigth in lands outside the Middle East where the first high gods dwell.<br /> <br /> These times saw humanity rising from the early ages of copper and stone to create some of the first great examples of what latter people's would call civilization and vampires were at the heart of it. Kings were defined by connection to the gods and religion was at the core of all life. So in this great and early time, the vampires could truly live as gods and why shouldn't they? Were they not immortal and filled with the divine blood of the high gods? How could they be anything but divine?<br /> <br /> Yet all things must end and so would this era. Many of these civilizations would fall in the Bronze Age Collapse and other analogous transition periods and so vampires are left to ask why.<br /> <br /> Was it merely the sudden shift of history due to natural factors? Or, as the Noddists posit, was the fiery collapses of these civilizations the punishment of The One for the hubris of vampire's claiming to be gods. Later years would see fewer examples of such activity, yet it was still prominent in the west into late antiquity and arguably still exists to some degree or another in the shadows of the modern nights.<br /> <br /> Yet time has passed on and for better or for worst, the nights of the Blood Divinities have come to their end, leaving only memories and dust in their wake...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}